{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "FM Slap Bass",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: the punchy, twangy digital 'slap' bass of 80s and early-90s pop and dance: a bright, metallic attack on a deep, clean note.\n\nHow it's built: FM synthesis. A sine modulator at the same pitch shakes the carrier sine (LIN FM) through its own VCA, opened by a very fast envelope: so only the first instant of each note is bright and twangy, and then it's a pure sine. A second envelope shapes the volume. One voice.\n\nPlay: funky, syncopated bass parts with octave jumps.\n\nTweak: the twang envelope's DECAY (longer is a 'bwow'), the carrier's LIN FM (how bright the slap), the modulator's OCTAVE.",
